d": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1010 and 883 are weakly connected only when time is ignored: their 2-hop neighbourhoods meet solely at the busy hub 1542, giving a minimum directed route of five hops (1010->66->1688/1824->1542->1209->883). Temporally, 1010 emits just one outgoing event (to 66) at ~70018-70517; 883's only inbound events are at ~62918-63917 (before the seed), ~70518-71517 and ~72518-73517. No ordered relay with <=600-unit gaps is evidenced across the intermediate hops, and the apparent connectivity is driven by hub popularity (1542 ~160 events, 1209 a star centre) rather than a time-respecting chain. Conclusion: no genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structural bottleneck.** In [51317, 89717] node 1010 has only **2 events** and node 883 only **3** (step_02) \u2014 both are peripheral, despite the window containing 6482 events (step_01). This rules out \"high volume \u21d2 cascade\" reasoning.\n\n**Directed reachability.** 1010's *only* outgoing neighbour is 66 (step_03); 883's incoming neighbours are 729, 1038, 1209 (step_04). The 2-hop neighbourhoods (step_05: {31,66,380,499,605,999,1429,1542,1688,1824,1952}; step_06: {149,296,356,459,487,582,729,971,990,1038,1090,1092,1116,1209,1343,1542,1561,1600,1937,1951}) intersect **only at 1542**. So the shortest *directed* route is 1010\u219266\u21921688/1824\u21921542\u21921209\u2192883 \u2014 **five hops**.\n\n**Temporal feasibility.** 1010's two events fall in [59118,60117] and [70018,70517] (step_08, step_14, step_15); the earlier one has no outgoing partner (step_12), so the *only* possible cascade seed is the single 1010\u219266 event at \u224870018\u201370517. 883's three incoming events are at \u2248[62918,63917], [70518,71517] and [72518,73517] (step_11, step_13, step_16). The first target event precedes the seed entirely. The remaining two lie 0\u20133000 units after the seed, but a 5-hop chain with \u2264600 per step must be threaded through the hub 1542 (\u2248160 events, step_10) and 1209 \u2014 no chained, ordered relay is evidenced, and the two candidate arrivals leave essentially no slack for five ordered hops. The high activity of 1542/1209 is a popularity confounder, not a relay.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_94b0ecbc\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883, 66, 1542, 1209],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1010 and 883 are weakly connected only when time is ignored: their 2-hop neighbourhoods meet solely at the busy hub 1542, giving a minimum directed route of five hops (1010->66->1688/1824->1542->1209->883). Temporally, 1010 emits just one outgoing event (to 66) at ~70018-70517; 883's only inbound events are at ~62918-63917 (before the seed), ~70518-71517 and ~72518-73517. No ordered relay with <=600-unit gaps is evidenced across the intermediate hops, and the apparent connectivity is driven by hub popularity (1542 ~160 events, 1209 a star centre) rather than a time-respecting chain. Conclusion: no genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40346, "total_output_tokens": 10036, "total_tokens": 50382, "total_latency_ms": 128511, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}